1
00:00:03,453 --> 00:00:09,024
Neural Networks by Hand and by PyTorch is
a companion book to a thirteen lesson
PyTorch curriculum.

2
00:00:09,074 --> 00:00:14,985
It is built so that you finish able to
read the literature and extend it, not
just reproduce a tutorial.

3
00:00:16,997 --> 00:00:19,133
Every idea appears in four registers.

4
00:00:19,183 --> 00:00:20,551
Derived as mathematics.

5
00:00:20,601 --> 00:00:22,146
Computed by hand on paper.

6
00:00:22,196 --> 00:00:24,450
Written as code you complete yourself.

7
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,112
And then mapped to the library call it
becomes in production.

8
00:00:29,923 --> 00:00:34,242
Chapter zero covers the four areas the
rest of the curriculum runs on.

9
00:00:34,292 --> 00:00:37,674
Linear algebra, calculus, statistics, and
probability.

10
00:00:37,724 --> 00:00:40,982
Every rule is verified in code rather than
asserted.

11
00:00:43,891 --> 00:00:48,414
Xavier initialisation is derived in three
lines from the variance of a sum.

12
00:00:48,464 --> 00:00:55,182
So is attention's one over root d k
scaling, and layer normalisation, and the
one over one minus p in dropout.

13
00:00:55,232 --> 00:00:56,646
These are not folklore.

14
00:00:56,696 --> 00:00:58,048
They are consequences.

15
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,367
There are seventeen interactive figures.

16
00:01:03,417 --> 00:01:06,749
Each one computes the same arithmetic as
the text beside it.

17
00:01:06,799 --> 00:01:09,465
Nothing here is drawn merely to look
convincing.

18
00:01:09,515 --> 00:01:13,234
Drag a slider, and the numbers move
because they were recalculated.

19
00:01:16,145 --> 00:01:19,885
Chapter zero alone carries twenty four
pencil and paper exercises.

20
00:01:19,935 --> 00:01:27,006
A gradient you have computed once with a
pencil stops being a symbol on a page, and
becomes a number you know how to check.

21
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:31,592
Every solution folds open underneath.

22
00:01:31,642 --> 00:01:36,085
The numbers are chosen so that arithmetic
never obscures the idea being drilled.

23
00:01:38,995 --> 00:01:43,372
Feedback said students struggle to
recognise which technique a problem needs.

24
00:01:43,422 --> 00:01:45,959
So the newest section is about exactly
that.

25
00:01:46,009 --> 00:01:50,615
Not computing a variance, but recognising
that something is a variance question.

26
00:01:50,665 --> 00:01:56,652
Four triggers, three guided diagnoses, and
drills where the answer is the category
rather than a number.

27
00:01:59,565 --> 00:02:03,469
From there the curriculum runs from XOR to
a working GPT.

28
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:16,026
Backpropagation by hand, convolutions,
LSTMs, attention, transformers,
translation, a decoder only language
model, and finally quantization and LoRA,
both implemented from scratch.

29
00:02:18,331 --> 00:02:19,838
And every claim is measured.

30
00:02:19,888 --> 00:02:23,786
The key value cache in chapter ten comes
out slower at notebook scale.

31
00:02:23,836 --> 00:02:32,349
Rather than quietly assert the textbook
answer, the book reports the wall clock
honestly, and adds an operation count that
explains why the two disagree.

32
00:02:34,353 --> 00:02:37,758
Every hand rolled component is then mapped
to the real thing.

33
00:02:37,808 --> 00:02:39,458
Scaled dot product attention.

34
00:02:39,508 --> 00:02:40,987
The peft library for LoRA.

35
00:02:41,037 --> 00:02:43,819
Hugging Face transformers for the language
model.

36
00:02:43,869 --> 00:02:48,464
Each with what the library adds, and just
as importantly, what it hides from you.

37
00:02:51,394 --> 00:02:54,437
The appendix aims past the end of the
curriculum.

38
00:02:54,487 --> 00:03:04,726
R M S norm, swiglu, rotary embeddings,
grouped query and latent attention,
mixture of experts, flash attention,
speculative decoding, and preference
optimisation.

39
00:03:04,776 --> 00:03:08,514
Each with the one line idea, and the
resource it buys back.

40
00:03:10,422 --> 00:03:12,378
And it makes the argument explicit.

41
00:03:12,428 --> 00:03:14,671
Almost none of that is new mathematics.

42
00:03:14,721 --> 00:03:20,117
Two of those entries are the low rank
factorisation you already implemented in
chapter eleven.

43
00:03:20,167 --> 00:03:23,155
Two more are the LSTM gating idea from
chapter five.

44
00:03:23,205 --> 00:03:25,276
The frontier is reachable from here.

45
00:03:27,193 --> 00:03:28,784
The book is a single page app.

46
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:34,582
Chapters are routes, cross references jump
instantly, and there is full text search
across every chapter.

47
00:03:34,632 --> 00:03:39,450
Follow a reference backwards and a button
returns you to exactly where you were
reading.

48
00:03:40,905 --> 00:03:43,939
Mathematics renders from a vendored copy
of KaTeX.

49
00:03:43,989 --> 00:03:48,010
No network, no content delivery network,
nothing external at all.

50
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:54,547
The whole book is a single file that
behaves identically served from a U R L or
opened straight off disk.

51
00:03:57,905 --> 00:04:00,327
So what should you be able to do
afterwards?

52
00:04:00,377 --> 00:04:02,798
Derive a loss function from a
distribution.

53
00:04:02,848 --> 00:04:06,955
Implement attention and check it
numerically against the library version.

54
00:04:07,005 --> 00:04:09,146
Diagnose why a network will not train.

55
00:04:09,196 --> 00:04:12,010
And read a paper, and reproduce its
central claim.

56
00:04:12,912 --> 00:04:15,600
And it holds you to a standard while you
do it.

57
00:04:15,650 --> 00:04:17,405
Matched parameter comparisons.

58
00:04:17,455 --> 00:04:19,968
Baselines tuned as hard as your own
method.

59
00:04:20,018 --> 00:04:21,774
Error bars over several seeds.

60
00:04:21,824 --> 00:04:24,453
And stating plainly what you cannot
conclude.

61
00:04:24,503 --> 00:04:28,880
There are five capstone projects,
including reproducing a published result.

62
00:04:31,189 --> 00:04:32,210
Thirteen lessons.

63
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:33,344
Fifteen chapters.

64
00:04:33,394 --> 00:04:37,439
Forty five by hand exercises, and
seventeen interactive figures.

65
00:04:37,489 --> 00:04:42,100
And all of it runs on a MacBook Air with
twenty four gigabytes of memory.
